{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/44050-chance-of-a-dark-ages-wraith-book","id":44050,"title":"Chance of a Dark Ages: Wraith book?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-07T02:46:09-08:00","id":44050,"title":"Chance of a Dark Ages: Wraith book?","content":"<span style=\"font-family:tahoma\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">With Wraith20 coming at the tail end of this year, I've slipped into a minor obsession with everyone's favorite game of dead guys having a bad time. I've always had a soft spot for historical settings, and Wraith got one (and a half, sort of; <i>The Great War </i>was a full setting, but <i>Ghost Towns</i> had some fun stuff for Wild West Wraith), but was left out of the whole <i>Dark Ages</i> business due to line being over by then. I was going to post a big rant here defending the notion, but found a small essay on the ancient (but nonetheless still good) WraithProject page that sums my thoughts up exactly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And we should see a Dark Ages: Wraith. Here's why:<br /> <br /> #1: It Fits the Time Frame. Perfectly: This is the Dark Ages. Reason is slow to stir, superstition rules the world and faith can make a heaven out of hell, or the reverse. The everpresent gloom lies outside the closing range of candle, flame and fire, and in that darkness lies the unknown - where threats and dangers to life and soul lurk and preen. Monsters are real, the ungodly waits for you and the only thing you can be sure of is a nasty, brutish and short lifespan...<br /> <br /> In other words, this time is the clay from which great ghost stories are made. The interplay of faith, supertition, belief has much to offer. And the everyday horror of life, pricked with minute spots of hope and joy, has too much great potential to ignore. When life is cheap and faith is so powerful, what else remains but death?<br /> <br /> #2: There Was Too Much Cool Stuff Going On, Then: The Second Great Maelstrom hadn't erupted yet. The Shadowlands and Tempest were not separated, yet, either. The Hierarchy was enjoying what could be called a &quot;golden age&quot; as their equitates patroled the dead roads leading to Stygia, and Legions all bristled with enthusiasm, and possibly even hope.<br /> <br /> Yes - hope. The great betrayal of the Fishers had yet to be discovered, though tensions mounted between the Crusaders and Charon. Transcendence was still the watchword of the Hierarchy's purpose; There was no state mandate to deny the promise it brings, which opens up all kinds of interesting avenues for roleplaying.<br /> <br /> The hope was marred by nay-sayers, of course. The Renegades had yet to gain strength, but they were still out there, waiting for a chance to attack lone Hierarchs on the way to the Isle. And while the Spectres might have been less numerous, the Labyrinth still had its plots and plans.<br /> <br /> Closer to home, not only were the Guilds not outlawed, but they were in the middle of the War between them. How much intrigue and action can come from that, alone?<br /> <br /> #3: Better Chance for Interaction: The Code of Charon isn't new, but the Shroud is much lower than it is in modern times (if it's even there at all...?). And the world is replete with &quot;Shallowings,&quot; where the lands of the living and the dead overlap, and a person can walk from one to the other by accident. Crossover aplenty for those who insist that Wraith's one, big failing was being too &quot;apart&quot; from the other WOD games... </div> </div> </div></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T04:29:18-08:00","id":44071,"title":"","content":"I love the idea of a Dark Ages: Wraith, and this post has some great points.<br /> It would be a very different game to the Wraith we know.<br /> The idea of a different Underworld cosmology is enough to get my imagination fire up, and the Arcanoi! How would they have looked back in the Dark Medieval?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I had a conscience once. Alas, I appear to have misplaced it.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1309-andreas-rayne","name":"Andreas Rayne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:01:49-08:00","id":44169,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">Before my troupe got Harrowed by Life, I was looking into a Dark Ages setting for Wraith. Nothing ever came of it (sadly) but the material on Hermitage Castle from <i>Haunts</i> was good inspiration. Oh, Johnny, you wacky bastage\u2026</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T08:43:30-08:00","id":44191,"title":"","content":"That would be a really cool idea. I know there's a 20th ed. made for the Dark Ages coming up so there will probably be a section for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T09:51:51-08:00","id":44249,"title":"","content":"There's a tantalising sidebar about Wraith in <b>Vampire: The Dark Ages</b>. It suggests that there would be more factions as player options, since Stygia wasn't quite yet the only game in town for the European dead. Also pre Dictum Mortuum, I think?<br /> <br /> I kind of remember someone at Onyx Path making a vague suggestion that <b>Dark Ages: Wraith</b> (and the published Dark Ages lines) were possibly-maybe-hypothetically-but-don't-get-your-hopes-up options as they go forward with the V20 Dark Ages line. But that was on the other forums, and so much speculation until they say something more definite. And until Wraith 20 comes out, I'd think...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T13:31:36-08:00","id":44403,"title":"","content":"Oh man...I would not be able to contain my excitement. Coming this fall Onyx Path: the taking of all my monies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1559-cryocube","name":"cryocube","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T18:57:42-08:00","id":44604,"title":"","content":"I think if you wanna get seriously historical, let's see Wraith: Ancient Rome. Let's see the beginnings of Charon's vision of the Shadowlands. Let's see the way the system was intended, maybe only the beginnings of the flaws, the corruption starting to wind its way in. The entire empire of Rome with its darker mirror in the Shadowlands. Let's see what it was like to be a Dead world Caesar, a soldier playing Lord of all Death.How different it must have been then, but will the same troubles that plague Stygia in the last age of Wraith. Let's see what it was like to get in on the ground floor of the great design before it all became a bureaucratic hell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-07T19:20:18-08:00","id":44610,"title":"","content":"While ancient Rome has its appeals, it\u2019s perhaps a bit too early for Wraith, in that the interesting stuff hasn\u2019t really started yet. By the time of the Dark Ages, the Hierarchy has been founded, the Guilds are in full force, etc. \u2014 only the Heretics are missing, though in their place you have the Fishers. Prior to the fall of Rome, you didn\u2019t have any of that: Stygia was still a Republic, the Hierarchy and the Guilds had not yet been founded, and the Fishers were latecomers to the Ancient Rome era.<br /> <br /> And yeah; no Dictum Mortuum yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T04:02:05-08:00","id":44800,"title":"","content":"On the one hand I can agree, DataW. But on the other, no one has done it. Sure the interesting stuff hasn't started yet, you could Play someone who Founds the Hierarchy, creates the Guilds, or just starts screwing it all up. Starts making the laws because the system is already getting shaky. Why play a game where you're trying to fight against everyone stabbing you in the back when you can be the one who starts it? Still, I see your point... Dark Ages has much more history going on to muddle around with and explore. I also feel DA has been done quite a lot. My interest lies in what Hasn't been done. Vampire had Dark Ages sure, but they also ventured into the Victorian era. Werewolf has Dark Ages, but they also tackled the Wild West. Maybe Wraith can have a Dark Ages as well, but which system has done Ancient Rome and which Other system would have reason to? Maybe perhaps, we can convince OPP that it would be worth doing both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/31/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><a href=\"http://glyphery.webs.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ut0SZ4h.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1332-darling_rose","name":"Darling_Rose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1332_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-08T06:17:33-08:00","id":44852,"title":"","content":"One thing at a time, IMHO. One thing I liked about the <b>Dark Ages: Vampire</b> relaunch in the early 2000s was that they quickly expanded it from a Vampire-centric setting to one that encompassed most of the gamelines: with <b>Dark Ages: Werewolf</b>, <b>Dark Ages: Mage</b>, <b>Dark Ages: Inquisitor</b>, <b>Dark Ages: Fae</b>, and <b>Devil\u2019s Due</b>, nearly every oWoD had a Dark Ages counterpart; the main exceptions are <b>Wraith</b> and <b>Mummy</b>; and the latter doesn\u2019t really need anything that wasn\u2019t already handled by <b>Mummy 2e</b>. <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s Dark Ages era, OTOH, is an incredibly dynamic point in the history of <b>Wraith</b> that has <i>not</i> been covered. <br /> <br /> Put another way: <b>Dark Ages</b> has certainly been done; but <b>Dark Ages: Wraith</b> is a glaring hole in both the <b>Dark Ages</b> coverage and <b>Wraith</b>\u2019s coverage. If I had to pick just one of Dark Ages or Ancient Rome to cover, I\u2019d want the former. And frankly, I\u2019d rather the <b>Wraith20</b> development team concentrate on modern day stuff; on the development side of things, another interesting possibility is that the <b>Dark Ages</b> developers could take on the main workload of a <b>Dark Ages: Wraith</b> book, with the <b>Wraith20</b> developers serving in a primarily advisory role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}